Requested by Cesar: "Make sure all collisions work correctly for any transplanted trees and the
bridge, and that they are all baked for the bots to take them into account."

TREES — no trees were transplanted by this task (bridges only; scenery_transplant is queued).
  TreeBakeValidator.ValidateAllHoles(): 18/18 PASS, run TWICE (before Stage C and after every
  scene save). Hole 07 1343 baked rows / 677 standalone. All five holes' tree_obstacles.csv and
  heightmap.bytes md5-identical to the iter-1 baseline above.

BRIDGE — Stage C built: BridgeObstacleData / Provider / Loader / Baker + BallSimulation wiring
  at all three phases + PhysicsLabController. bridge_obstacles.csv hole 07 = 95 boxes
  (bake_hash 16583aa6): 118 railing + 10 pier harvested, 6 deck-slab excluded, 33 LOD duplicates
  dropped.

THREE DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED IN MY OWN BAKER (audited as one shape, per CLAUDE.md rule 15):
  1. per-collider yaw frame -> inflated diagonal truss members; blocking faces landed at
     +1.820 / -2.484 against railing art symmetric at +/-2.26. Fixed: reduce every box in the
     BRIDGE's frame, and derive yaw as atan2(across.z, across.x) to match BridgeBox.ToLocalXZ.
  2. +/-0.15 m "straddling" band swallowed the KERB boxes (top 24.007 vs deck 23.947, 0.060 m
     proud). Ball rolled off at 2.404 m, 0.095 m short of the railing, and fell 23.7 m.
     Fixed: above-deck band tightened to +0.02 m.
  3. colliders exist on BOTH LOD levels -> every box baked twice (124 rows / 93 unique).
     Fixed: dedupe on the formatted row.

MEASURED AFTER THE FIXES (deck half-width 2.404 m):
  ball rolled off the centreline at 2/4/6/8/10/14/20 m/s, BOTH directions: 14/14 end ON the
  bridge at Y 23.92-23.98, stopped at |perp| ~2.00 m. Same 14 with bridges=null: 14/14 in Water
  at Y 0.24. Approach shots landing at 0.0/0.5/1.0/1.5/2.0 m off-centre: all end on the bridge.
  Determinism: two identical shots bit-identical (242 samples, raw fp equal).

TESTS: 22 EditMode assemblies, 1962 passed, 0 failed, 3 pre-existing skips.
  23 BridgeCollisionTests, incl. Sim_BridgesNull_IsBitExactWithThePreStageCPath.

BOTS — measured A/B over 205 points on the bridge footprint (current zones.json vs the same bake
  with the Bridge group removed): IsPlayableSurface changed on 26 points, IsAvoidSurface on 20.
  So the SPEC's "zero change to bot behaviour" claim is NOT what happens. See report.

