=== iter-3 2026-08-31 (Cesar: "Add bots + bridges, author railing boxes, explain hole 12,
    re-run tree drift and then commit if everything checks out") ===

BOTS + BRIDGES — decision taken. VersusBot.IsAvoidSurface now returns true for Bridge as well as
  Water. Being absent from IsPlayableSurface was only half the job: that governs what the bot
  TARGETS, while IsAvoidSurface is what the H2 hazard/lay-up path keys off. Test renamed to
  Bots_TreatABridgeAsAHazardAndNeverTargetIt and now asserts BOTH predicates plus that Water /
  Fairway / Sand are unaffected. This is the one edit to VersusBot; the SPEC listed it out of
  scope and Cesar authorised it explicitly.

RAILING BOXES for bridgeLODs.fbx (holes 8 x2, 9) — SPEC Risk 2 closed, but NOT by a prefab
  variant. Assets/Packs/ is gitignored (.gitignore:107), so a hand-authored variant beside the
  FBX would never leave this machine — same class of bug as the gitignored hole scenes. Instead
  BridgeObstacleBaker gained a renderer-AABB fallback: when a model ships zero BoxColliders it
  derives one box per railing/pier member (Railing_/Top_/Beams_L_/Beams_R_/Pier_/End_/Bottom_),
  skipping sparse geometry (StreetLight_Poles 0.97x8.21x46.5 of mostly air, Line, the 1 mm
  Fence planes) and the deck. Output lands in the TRACKED bridge_obstacles.csv, no new asset.
  VERIFIED on the real FBX in a throwaway in-memory scene at hole 9's ground-truth TRS:
    0 BoxColliders confirmed; 12 boxes derived (8 railing + 4 pier);
    deck edges -2.404..+2.404 m, railing inner faces -2.256 / +2.260 m
    -> CONTAINED on both sides, without needing the kerbs hole 7 depended on.
  Temp deck asset deleted, scene discarded unsaved.

REGRESSION — hole 7 bridge_obstacles.csv re-baked after the refactor: md5
  3b23c5dfbe5fd6bd7a0ea03b2638cf98, bake_hash 16583aa6 — IDENTICAL. The collider path is
  untouched by the fallback.

HOLE 12 — no deadlock is structurally possible: TrySafeLanding is a bounded search (walk back in
  LayupStep increments, then OffsetDegrees rotated lines) with an explicit else branch that logs
  "no safe landing found - using original line (reactive OBReason will catch)". So the SPEC's
  deadlock worry cannot hang the bot. What the IsAvoidSurface change DOES do is make that
  fallback fire more often on hole 12. Still outstanding for hole 12 (not transplanted yet):
  two bridges, both x-tilted (5.22 deg and 1.79 deg) - the first exercise of tilt in the deck
  generator and the per-box BaseY/TopY fold - and SPEC Risk 1 (nothing can pass UNDER a deck).

