=== iter-4 2026-08-31 — ALL 7 BRIDGES, holes 8 / 9 / 12 / 17 batched ===

TRANSPLANT — 6 remaining instances, all at max |dpos|=0.000000 m, max dangle=0.000000 deg,
  max |dscale|=0.000000 against the Video source (33/17/27/27/14 transforms compared, 0 unmatched).
  Positions and scales match the SPEC ground-truth table row for row, x-tilts included
  (hole 12: 5.22 and 1.79 deg; hole 17: 0.36 deg).

zones.json — every hole gained EXACTLY one Bridge group (hole 8 and 12 with 2 polygons, one per
  bridge); no other group's polygon/vert/tri counts moved and every obMask is byte-identical.

TWO MORE DEFECTS, both only reachable through the x-tilt — which is exactly why hole 12 mattered:
  4. Classification sampled the deck ONCE at each box's centre. On a tilted bridge a 40.8 m deck
     slab has its global maxY at the high END, 4.5 m above the deck under its middle, so the DECK
     SLAB ITSELF was filed as a railing: 3 boxes of halfX 2.404 (exactly the deck half-width) and
     halfZ 20.4, a solid block standing on the walkway. Fixed by measuring each corner against the
     deck directly beneath THAT corner.
  5. That per-corner sample then fell through to the deck's MEAN Y outside the footprint — and the
     slab's corners sit exactly ON the boundary, so the tilt error came straight back. Fixed by
     falling back to the nearest deck vertex, which carries the tilt with it.
  Regression proof: holes 7, 8 and 9 (level decks) re-bake BYTE-IDENTICAL through both fixes.

SEAL CHECK — whether a model's own colliders stop a ball ROLLING off its deck turned out to vary
  per model, so it is now measured per side per bridge and repaired only where it fails:
    Bridge_withLODs  sealed by model  (kerbs at +/-2.004 inside edges +/-2.404)
    bridgeLODs       sealed by model  (railing slab at +/-2.256 / +/-1.128)
    Bridge_part_1    UNSEALED         (colliders -2.555/2.488, outboard of +/-2.404) -> hole 17
      measured 0 of 8 rolls staying on the deck. Its railing IS baked at inner face 2.269, but its
      BASE is 23.791 over a deck of 23.62-23.71, so it floats 0.10-0.17 m up and a 43 mm ball rolls
      underneath. Repaired with 2 SYNTHESIZED KERB boxes spanning deck -> railing base over the
      railing's own footprint. This is the ONE piece of geometry in this task not taken from the
      art; logged by the baker and flagged in the report.

CONTAINMENT, all 7 bridges: 8/8 perpendicular rolls (3/6/10/16 m/s x both directions) end ON the
  bridge, mid-deck classifies as Bridge, SampleHeight returns the deck.

